{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>you cannot behold Him</b> — even though you have no ability to see the Place." "<b>your case is before Him, and you wait for Him</b> — like קוה. And some say: it is from חיל, and the meaning is bearing strength on His account, as in: \"Be silent to HaShem and wait for Him [והתחולל לו]\" (Psalms 37:7)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra cites two derivations for ותחולל: from the root קוה (to wait/hope), or from חיל (strength), with the sense of bearing or directing one's strength toward Him. The gloss 'like קוה' indicates the first reading takes it as a byform of ותקוה."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:37.954012593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}